H3746.def:
A group, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 8:18; also called Carite at 2 Rois 11:4,19; 
Group of ke.re.ti (כְּרֵתִי "Cherethite" H3774H) 
a group of foreign mercenary soldiers serving as a bodyguard for king David; also executioners

H3756H.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at Josué 7:1; 
son of: Zabdi (H2067); 
father of: Achan (H5912)
§ Carmi = "my vineyard"
1) the 4th son of Reuben and progenitor of the Carmites
2) a Judaite, father of Achan, the 'troubler of Israel' in the time of Joshua

H3756I.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 2:9; 
son of: Hezron (H2696H); 
brother of: Ram (H7410), Jerahmeel (H3396), Segub (H7687H) and Ashhur (H0806); married to Azubah (H5806H), Jerioth (H3408), Ephrathah (H0672), Ephah (H5891H) and Maacah (H4601L); 
father of: Hur (H2354), Jesher (H3475), Shobab (H7727H), Ardon (H0715), Mareshah@1 Chroniques 2:42 (H4337), Haran (H2771B), Moza (H4162), Gazez (H1495), Jahdai (H3056), Sheber (H7669), Tirhanah (H8647), Shaaph (H8174H), Sheva (H7724) and Achsah (H5915H); also called Carmi (NIV: Karmi) at 1 Chroniques 4:1(?); Chelubai at 1 Chroniques 2:9; 
Another name of ka.lev (כָּלֵב "Caleb" H3612H)
§ Carmi = "my vineyard"
1) the 4th son of Reuben and progenitor of the Carmites
2) a Judaite, father of Achan, the 'troubler of Israel' in the time of Joshua

H3757.def:
Someone descended from Carmi who was a man of the tribe of Reuben living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Genèse 46:9; 
son of: Reuben (H7205); 
brother of: Pallu (H6396), Hezron (H2696) and Hanoch (H2585J)
Group of kar.mi (כַּרְמִי "Carmi" H3756) 
§ Carmi = "my vineyard"
the Carmites descended from the 4th son of Reuben

H3763.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 36:26; 
son of: Dishon (H1787); 
brother of: Eshban (H0790), Ithran (H3506) and Hemdan (H2533) 
§ Cheran = "lyre"
an Edomite, one of the sons of Dishon, the Horite duke

H3777.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, only mentioned at Genèse 22:22; 
son of: Nahor (H5152H) and Milcah (H4435); 
brother of: Uz (H5780H), Buz (H0938), Kemuel (H7055), Hazo (H2375), Pildash (H6394), Jidlaph (H3044) and Bethuel (H1328A); 
half-brother of: Tebah (H2875), Gaham (H1514), Tahash (H8477) and Maacah (H4601) 
§ Chesed = "increase"
the 4th son of Nahor, the nephew of Abraham
